        "name": "Gerrit AI review for Lustre",
        "display_name": "AI review",
        "email": "gaireview@linuxhacker.ru",
        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-10-05 16:56:56.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(6 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. The removed check also caught max_brw == 0 and acted as the only bound on client-supplied nfrags before the bd_vec allocation, so removing it outright re-exposes both. Keeping a relaxed check (e.g. against LNET_MAX_IOV * PTLRPC_BULK_OPS_COUNT, plus max_brw == 0) would fix the reconnect ENOMEM without that. A regression test would also help: lower obdfilter.*.brw_size, force a client reconnect with large dirty extents cached, and check the writes complete.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
