          "date": "2026-10-05 09:20:18.000000000",
          "tz": 180
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Alexey Lyashkov",
          "email": "alexey.lyashkov@hpe.com",
          "date": "2026-10-17 07:43:11.000000000",
          "tz": 180
        },
        "subject": "LU-20875 ptlrpc: let be less strict for max frags",
        "message": "LU-20875 ptlrpc: let be less strict for max frags\n\nThe server might reduce the maximum bulk size after the initial\nconnection, and this could cause large extents to be created\nand prepared for sending. Therefore, it might exceed the current\nlimit. Let's make the bulk size checking less strict.\n\nInstead of rejecting the whole bulk descriptor at creation time, do\nthe capacity check in the place which knows the real descriptor state.\nadd_kiov_frag() was declared void, so a fragment which does not fit\ncould only be reported with an LASSERT, and both limit checks were\ndone after the store, so an out of bounds write into bd_vec[] or\nbd_mds_off[] happened before the panic.\n\nCheck the bd_max_iov and PTLRPC_BULK_OPS_LIMIT bounds before storing,\nreturn -EOVERFLOW instead, and make every add_kiov_frag() caller fail\nthe RPC.\n\nFixes: e1ac9e74 (\"LU-10157 ptlrpc: fill md correctly.\")\nHPe-bug-id: LUS-13418\nSigned-off-by: Alexey Lyashkov <alexey.lyashkov@hpe.com>\nChange-Id: I66a3956a607074bb2938f109811c321375b8fd28\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
